  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract activity in Kentucky through FY2027 to date is concentrated and small compared with recent years. Total obligations are $59.5M across 188 awards, with an average award size of $316K. Federal obligations are down 99.3% year over year. Historical annual obligations show a peak range: FY22 was $11.9B, FY23 was $12.5B, FY24 was $12.3B, FY25 was $10.4B, and FY26 was $9.1B, before the FY27 to date total of $59.5M. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer in FY2027 to date at $39.5M, followed by the Department of the Treasury at $17.9M and the Department of Agriculture at $1.2M. WIELAND ROLLED PRODUCTS NORTH AMERICA, LLC is the largest vendor in FY2027 to date at $17.9M, followed by UNIVERSITY OF LOUISVILLE at $7.1M and PDS CONSULTANTS, INC at $5.2M. Copper Rolling, Drawing, Extruding, and Alloying is the largest NAICS industry at $17.9M, and Colleges, Universities, and Professional Schools is next at $7.4M. Current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
